topics.detail:
AI Not Wanted argues that AI is unwanted or problematic. AI Advancements argues that AI leaps over complex gateways. AI clarifies the tech industry. AI enables a unified security layer. AI proves a 31-year-old math problem.

@skyladawn.ca: “So interestingly the "but with AI..." people tend to be other writers who don't care about worker solidarity--the readers wanting more audiobooks all want humans. (But yes I have blocked a lot of people who would say that lol)”

AI Not Wanted (76.7%) says AI is unwanted or problematic. AI Advancements (23.3%) says AI achieves significant breakthroughs.

Technology.detail:
AI Agents argues that AI agents reuse verified answers with Navige. AI agents run code in E2B sandboxes. AI agents build apps with natural language prompts using Bolt. AI Free Space argues that Writers need a site without AI. Artists need a new platform to escape AI. AI Bubble argues that AI lending will collapse. Hyperscalers' debt funding is unsustainable. Debt-fueled AI spending has limits.

@praefix.bsky.social: “I'm not trying to make anyone feel bad here but it's just some food for thought to consider maybe if you're trying to make community with artists who don't want to see AI in their art spaces, a good start is not mentioning it every time you bring up your or anyone elses'…”

AI Agents (80%) says AI agents are improved with new tools. AI Free Space (10%) says Artists need a space without AI. AI Bubble (10%) says AI spending is unsustainable.

Health.detail:
Universal Healthcare argues that Universal healthcare is needed to replace the expensive system. Opposition to free healthcare is selfish. The US prioritizes military spending over universal healthcare. The current system prioritizes insurance over healthcare. Universal coverage with a single payer is the best delivery method. Denial of healthcare is justified by the wealthy to maintain their power. Universal Healthcare argues that Single-payer systems involve tradeoffs. Canada's system is cost-effective.

@publicuniversal.bsky.social: “Like “American healthcare works for most people most of the time…but when it does fail it fails catastrophically and if you fall through the cracks you are turbofucked” explains both why it sucks and why fixing it is politically difficult pretty well.”

Universal Healthcare (54.4%) says the US needs universal healthcare. Universal Healthcare (45.6%) says Universal healthcare is better.

Covid Vaccines argues that Vaccines are effective against Covid. Covid vaccines are a safe choice. Vaccine Mandate argues that Not vaccinating children is abuse.

@crshort81.bsky.social: “Start of COVID and now.”

Covid Vaccines (50.7%) says Get vaccinated for Covid. Vaccine Mandate (49.3%) says Not vaccinating children is abuse.

Vaccine Side Effects argues that Vaccines cause immediate illness. Mood Shifts argues that I felt terrible but now I feel great. I'm anxious but made it through.

@birdapp.rip: “I wonder why I feel like complete shit today it couldnt possibly be the fact that I gamed until 2am and got maybe 5 hours of sleep? nah, couldnt be that”

Vaccine Side Effects (64.3%) says Vaccines cause immediate illness. Mood Shifts (35.7%) says People experience sudden changes in their mood.
